# T218 — measured-fit table (A6 fit leg, v3.1) · FINAL build (post-cure) sha256 50b854e7ca8b2cec267e94a698154578823c812bd69f24bdc3204a3b6c28c182 · 16,968 B

- **Instrument:** PIL (Pillow) rendered text measurement — `ImageFont.getbbox` on each string rendered at 4× its CONFIG size and divided back, Regular weight throughout. **PROXY stand-in font: DejaVu Serif** (`/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSerif.ttf`) standing in for the CONFIG `fontFamily` stack (Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif), which is not installed in this seat. Every width/height below is a rendered measurement of that proxy, never a character-width model. DejaVu Serif is wider than Georgia for most strings, so width overflows are conservative (worst-case direction); ink heights transfer closely.
- **Filing history:** this table REPLACES the prewave firing-1 table in full. The firing-1 table's geometry record was incomplete (jev-prewave finding 3: zone names without numeric container bounds or binding margins) and its tile widths were measured against a superseded slot/font state; the table below is a complete re-measure on the final build with per-row container bounds and signed stage margins. The font-cure history stands: first-pass CONFIG fonts (headers 30/17, centre 17/16, enslaved 16, tile min 20) measured 7.9–11.2 px ink @360 and were raised in CONFIG (campSub 24 · centre 23/22 · enslaved 22 · tile min 26, scale 0.22, per-tile overrides Pennsylvania/Massachusetts 24).
- **Floor:** ink height at 360 px phone width (stage 640 → ×0.5625); the fleet's working floor is ~11 px ink. Rows at or under it are HITs.
- Tile-label container = the tile's own free box (freeW × freeH); zone containers as listed. Span = proxy ink centred at CONFIG cx; margR = 640 − spanR (negative = past the stage's right edge); spanL negative = past the left edge.

