## HITs (carried, with dispositions)
1. **Ink-height floor proximity — tile labels.** Minimum ink @360 = 10.41 px (Massachusetts, 18.5 stage px); Connecticut 11.1, North/South Carolina 11.25, New York 11.4 — the tile labels sit at 95–104% of the ~11 px floor. Disposition: CARRIED — the floor pressure is set by the specimen's own small tiles at phone width; fonts are already at the containment ceiling for the two widest names (overrides at 24 px). Priced again at the readability lens.
2. **Pennsylvania proxy stage overflow.** 159.0 px proxy ink centred at cx 566 spans 486.5–645.5 → right margin **−5.5 px** past the 640 stage edge. Disposition: CARRIED — proxy-dependent (DejaVu wider than Georgia); the label is centred on its tile exactly as the specimen's right-edge labels are; PIXEL-UNVERIFIED in this seat.
3. **Massachusetts proxy stage overflow.** 180.2 px proxy ink centred at cx 562 spans 471.9–652.1 → right margin **−12.1 px**. Disposition: CARRIED — same basis as HIT 2; the 24 px override already trades ink height (HIT 1) against this width.
4. **Delaware proxy left-edge touch.** 125.5 px proxy ink centred at cx 62 spans −0.8–124.8 → left margin **−0.8 px**. Disposition: CARRIED — sub-pixel under the proxy; same PIXEL-UNVERIFIED basis.
5. **Tile-label box-overflow class.** Nine tile labels (North Carolina, South Carolina, Delaware, Maryland, Georgia, New Jersey, New York, Connecticut, New Hampshire) measure wider than their own free boxes — the label is centred on the tile and extends over the map ground, exactly as the specimen's state names sit across the map (several specimen names are wider than their tiles). Disposition: PRICED IN PLAN §2.5 as the specimen's own behaviour — labels ride the ground with a halo; tiles are row-separated (row bands ≥44 px apart in cy against ≤28.2 px ink height) so centred labels cannot collide with a neighbouring row's label. Carried as a class, PIXEL-UNVERIFIED.
# T218 — config census (A6 config-census leg, v3.1) · final build sha256 50b854e7ca8b2cec267e94a698154578823c812bd69f24bdc3204a3b6c28c182 (census re-verified on the cured build: the prewave cure round changed two CONFIG values — tFreeMs/freeDurMs — and no keys, literals or sites; the key→site table below is unchanged)

## §1 All-literal scan (outside the CONFIG block)
- Hex colors outside CONFIG: `#e9e6de` (page chrome body background) + `#1a1a1a` (page chrome body text) — page chrome, not subject: classified **structural/chrome** (the scene's ground and ink come from `palette.*`). No other hex/rgba outside CONFIG.
- Logic-script numbers: `0, 0.5, 1, 2` — clamp01 bounds, easing coefficient, halving for phase midpoints: **structural** (mathematical identities). `3, 5, 7` — string slice indices in `hexRgb` (hex channel extraction): **structural**. `20` — the validateConfig fit-floor form constant (`tileLabelMinPx >= 20` rejects a CONFIG whose minimum label font falls below the floor form; the CONFIG value itself is 26): **structural** (guard constant, shapes no rendered value directly).
- Render-script numbers: `0, 1, 2` — indices/bounds: **structural**. `4` — the centre-label second-line leading offset (`fontPx + 4` in makeLabelGroup): a fixed typographic leading offset, classified **structural** (it shapes no subject value; line spacing for tile labels is CONFIG `labelLineHeight`). `0.35` — text baseline alignment factor (`fontPx * 0.35` centres label ink on the tile centre): **structural** typographic constant. `100` — SVG pathLength dash normalization identity: **structural**. `1000` — ms→s clock display: **structural**. `2000`-class strings: none (the scan's digit hits inside identifiers like `t218` are not literals).
- CSS numbers: page-chrome layout only (max-width 680, paddings, button min-height 44 — fleet tappability chrome). **Structural.**
- Font stack in CSS (`Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif` on body) is page chrome; the scene's text reads CONFIG `fontFamily` at its sites. No subject-shaping literal stands outside CONFIG. (Arrow geometry literals found in the first draft — head size 9, spread 0.42, curve lift 18 — were BOUND into CONFIG as `arrowHeadPx`/`arrowHeadSpread`/`arrowLiftPx` before this census was filed; the census above is of the final build.)

