**Motion findings:** motion instants — map highlight sweep ≈0–6000 ms (lead-in, not the technique) · tile fade-in ≈6000–8000 ms · free growth ≈9000–11000 ms (280–282 s) with arrows drawn by 10000 ms and the label completing with the growth · free label/arrows removal ≈16000–17000 ms (287–288 s) · enslaved frames ≈20000–21000 ms (291–292 s) · enslaved label reveal ≈21000–22000 ms, its removal ≈24000–27000 ms (295–298 s). Holds — small-tile ≈8000–9000 ms · free state with label ≈11000–16000 ms · bare free ≈17000–20000 ms · enslaved state ≈22000–28000 ms. No tile changes camp, ever; the two acts are (1) tile AREA re-set to free population, (2) a FRAME added around South tiles whose thickness carries enslaved population. Tile colour shifts dark grey (small state) → teal (free state) during the growth.
**Camp assignment (census-priced):** 12 tiles. South camp (left + centre columns): Virginia · North Carolina · South Carolina · Delaware · Maryland · Georgia · New Jersey (7 — New Jersey stands in the centre column grouped with the Carolinas, on the South half of the stage). North camp (right half): New York · Pennsylvania · Connecticut · Massachusetts · New Hampshire (5). Rhode Island does not appear.
**Size/frame values: VISUAL ESTIMATES** — free sizes and frame thicknesses estimated from the census/ev frames at 640 px against the Pennsylvania anchor (largest free tile); no per-state population table is supplied by the packet, and no measured area-to-population scaling rule is claimed.
**Sub-beats:** SB-A tile fade-in at small size + headers · SB-B growth to free-population area + grey→teal shift, arrows draw · SB-C free label completes with growth · SB-D free label/arrows removal (bare free hold) · SB-E enslaved frames grow on South tiles · SB-F enslaved label reveal, then its removal · SB-G final hold (frames only).

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Tile set — per tile: label, camp (south/north), centre position, free width/height (area carries free population), enslaved frame thickness (0 for North tiles).
2. Camp headers — title + subtitle text per camp, header positions, title/sub font sizes.
3. Small state — smallFraction (tile scale in SB-A), tinyFraction (fade-in start scale), appearStartOpacity (mid-fade opacity at the allocation zero), tile start fill (dark grey) → free fill (teal).
4. Centre labels — free label lines, enslaved label text, label font sizes/positions, arrow schedules (arrows draw on their own phase), arrow apex points, arrow target tiles (by label name, camp fallback), arrow colours/widths.
5. Timing — appear, free-growth, arrows, free-label, free-label-out, enslaved-frames, enslaved-label, enslaved-label-out starts/durations, final hold, total duration.
6. Palette — paper ground, tile grey, tile teal, enslaved rust, ink, label ink, arrow teal, arrow ink, tile-label white.
7. Tile labels — font family, per-tile font rule (scale with tile width, min/max clamps), line-height, halo width, wrap rule (words stacked, max 2 lines).
8. Easing — per-phase easing names.
9. Phase order — appear < free growth; arrows + free label inside the growth window; label-out after growth; enslaved frames after label-out; enslaved label after frames; its removal last (validation-enforced, §2.1).

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent (runtime sampling of config-rendered text): NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; all text is DOM/SVG text rendered from CONFIG strings, the same config-driven principle in its DOM form. Reason stated here per A9.5.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2 (intensity separation · phrase exclusivity): NOT APPLICABLE as particle/sequence cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is construction-level: the two counting rules are different KINDS of mark (area vs frame), never the same mark at two intensities; and the two acts are strictly sequential by the phase-order invariant (Owner Cure 2's exclusivity in schedule form).
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool exists in this technique.
- A9.1 plate construction: NOT APPLICABLE — no moving background plate; the ground is the specimen's still paper ground.
- Family: Packet #12 tile/diagram siblings — T210 grid-map PASS 85.2 (five lenses 72/90/98/78/88, motion minimum) · T212 margin bars NO VERDICT (receipt-form cures). **Sibling cures carried into this item's Plan (jev-observe-exit cure, applied):** T210's completion cures — CONFIG-dependent probes whose instants MOVE under a timing swap · whole-state equality probes · palette swap verified in rendered output · receipt-index reconciliation — and T212's three priced cures — every census checkpoint's evaluation instant as a CONFIG expression (or a census-fixed probe whose evaluated STATE is CONFIG-derived and shown to move under the swap) · raw phase value and eased result printed as separately identified values · full-predicate receipts (every tile, not samples) — are all binding on §2.3/§2.4 below and on the build-record's RECEIPT INDEX (A13).

## §2 — PLAN (AS AMENDED at §2b — all gate cures applied in this text)

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · headerY 18 · campTitleFontPx 30 · campSubFontPx 17 · centreLabelFontPx 21 · centreSubFontPx 14 · enslavedLabelFontPx 20 · tileLabelScale 0.17 · tileLabelMinPx 20 · tileLabelMaxPx 30 · labelLineHeight 1.15 · labelHaloPx 3 · tinyFraction 0.18 · smallFraction 0.5 · appearStartOpacity 0.55 · arrowWidthPx 3.5 · arrowApex [0.50,0.27] · enslavedArrowApex [0.64,0.27] · freeArrowTargets ["North Carolina","New York"] · enslavedArrowTarget "North Carolina" · tAppearMs 0 · appearDurMs 1500 · headerDurMs 800 · tFreeMs 2500 · freeDurMs 2500 · tArrowsMs 3000 · arrowsDurMs 1000 · tFreeLabelMs 3500 · freeLabelDurMs 1500 · tFreeLabelOutMs 10000 · freeLabelOutDurMs 1000 · tEnslavedMs 14000 · enslavedDurMs 1000 · tEnslavedLabelMs 15000 · enslavedLabelDurMs 1000 · tEnslavedLabelOutMs 17500 · enslavedLabelOutDurMs 1000 · holdMs 2500 · easeAppear/easeFree/easeLabel/easeEnslaved all "easeInOut" · palette {ground #f4f1ea, tileStart #4a4a4a, tile #56706b, enslaved #c85a2e, ink #333333, labelInk #2f2f2f, arrowFree #6fa8a0, arrowDark #2f2f2f, tileLabel #ffffff} · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" · campSouthTitle "South" · campSouthSub "Pro-slavery" · campNorthTitle "North" · campNorthSub "Anti-slavery" · campSouthX 160 · campNorthX 490 · freeLabelLine1 "Free people population" · freeLabelLine2 "(mostly white)" · freeLabelX 320 · freeLabelY 92 · enslavedLabelText "Enslaved people" · enslavedLabelX 415 · enslavedLabelY 92`.
Derived (named, not stored): tile scale at t (tiny→small→free interpolation) · tile fill (tileStart→tile lerp by eased free progress) · frame thickness = enslavedPx × eased enslaved progress · freeLabelOpacity (in by label phase, out by label-out phase) · enslavedLabelOpacity (in by its phase, out by its out-phase) · arrow endpoints — resolved at derive time from the CONFIG target labels (tile of that label, else the first tile of that label's camp in the specimen camp map, else the first tile of the camp) to the target tile's current top-edge point; apex from the CONFIG apex fractions × stage · completeAtMs = tEnslavedLabelOutMs + enslavedLabelOutDurMs = 18500 · durationMs = completeAtMs + holdMs = 21000. **Phase-order invariant (validation-enforced, tightened at §2b):** all durations > 0 and finite; tFreeMs ≥ appear end; tFreeMs ≤ tArrowsMs and arrows end ≤ free end; tFreeMs ≤ tFreeLabelMs and free-label end ≤ free end; tFreeLabelOutMs ≥ free end; tEnslavedMs ≥ free-label-out end; tEnslavedLabelMs ≥ enslaved-frames end; tEnslavedLabelOutMs ≥ enslaved-label end — a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped. Negative probes: tFreeLabelMs→7000 REJECTED (label end 8500 > free end 5000) · tEnslavedMs→9000 REJECTED (before label-out end 11000). Boundary probe: tEnslavedMs = 11000 (= label-out end) ACCEPTED.
Nested: `tiles[12]` — `{label, camp, cx, cy, freeW, freeH, enslavedPx}` (sizes/thicknesses are the §1.3 VISUAL ESTIMATES at the 640 px stage; positions AMENDED at §2b so no two tiles overlap at full size — geometry assertion in the harness): Virginia south 100,165 140×135 e15 · North Carolina south 240,144 118×118 e11 · South Carolina south 240,252 84×84 e8 · Delaware south 62,262 44×44 e3 · Maryland south 140,282 96×96 e8 · Georgia south 62,330 58×58 e4 · New Jersey south 232,338 84×84 e3 · New York north 428,168 124×120 e0 · Pennsylvania north 566,145 144×138 e0 · Connecticut north 380,278 88×94 e0 · Massachusetts north 562,275 132×120 e0 · New Hampshire north 462,345 66×84 e0. (Count assertion: tiles source-count 12 = built-count 12, harness-printed. Frame-collision rule: frames draw BEHIND tiles, so a frame extending under a neighbour tile is hidden there — the specimen's frames abut the same way; the harness asserts tile-vs-tile non-overlap at full size and every frame's extent inside the stage.)
Derived (never stored): per-tile scale, fill, frame thickness, label font px = clamp(freeW × tileLabelScale, tileLabelMinPx, tileLabelMaxPx).

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG tiles + frames (chosen):** one SVG scene; per tile a frame rect (enslaved colour, drawn behind, grown outward by frame thickness) + a tile rect + centred wrapped text label (words stacked ≤2 lines, halo via paint-order stroke); two camp header groups; centre label groups with SVG arrow paths whose endpoints resolve from CONFIG target tiles (dash draw-on for the free arrows on their own phase, fade+draw for the enslaved arrow) — all geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement + DOM label measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). HTML div tiles — workable, but SVG gives exact rect/frame geometry for harness receipts at less code.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) the colonial-map lead-in (source 271–277 s) — a different visual device (antique map + highlight sweep), not the tile technique; the build opens on the paper ground at the tile lifecycle, and the comparison holds the build's zero state through the lead-in, labeled as the allocation on its face. (2) State-silhouette glyphs inside tiles — omitted: drawing state outlines from the specimen frames would approach tracing, and the technique's mechanic is area/frame re-categorisation, carried by tile size, frame, and the state NAME label. (3) The three-fifths banner/person at the window tail (source ≈298–305 s) — T219's technique, queue item #101; the comparison holds the build's final state through the tail, labeled likewise.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **t=0 allocation** — build 0 ms = source 277000 ms (segment-relative 6000 ms); build instant = census seg-rel − 6000 for every tile-lifecycle checkpoint. Departure table: census CP0–CP2 (map lead-in, 0–4000 ms) and CP14–CP17 (T219 tail, 28000–34000 ms) have NO build counterpart — named deferrals §2.2 (1) and (3). Census CP3 (6000 ms) maps to build 0 as a MID-FADE state (tiny tiles visible) — the build-zero assertion is therefore renamed **Z0** (never "CP0") and prescribes opacity = CONFIG appearStartOpacity, not zero; there is no zero-state tile anchor in this window (guards cmd 8 discharged by Z0 + this departure line).
Assertions (each: CONFIG expression → evaluated instant; every receipt prints the raw phase value and the eased result as separately identified values, and full predicates over ALL tiles — T212 cures, §1.5):
- Z0 build zero: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tAppearMs)` → 0 ms: every tile opacity = appearStartOpacity (0.55), scale = tinyFraction (0.18); headers opacity 0.
- P1 appear complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tAppearMs + CONFIG.appearDurMs)` → 1500 ms: every tile scale = smallFraction, opacity 1; headers 1.
- P2 free mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeMs + CONFIG.freeDurMs/2)` → 3750 ms: raw phase 0.5, eased 0.5; every tile scale = 0.5 + 0.5×0.5 = 0.75; fill lerp 0.5.
- P3 free complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeMs + CONFIG.freeDurMs)` → 5000 ms: every tile scale 1; freeLabelP 1; arrowsP 1.
- P4 label-out mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeLabelOutMs + CONFIG.freeLabelOutDurMs/2)` → 10500 ms: freeLabelOpacity 0.5.
- P5 bare hold: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFreeLabelOutMs + CONFIG.freeLabelOutDurMs)` → 11000 ms: freeLabelOpacity 0; every frame 0.
- P6 enslaved mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tEnslavedMs + CONFIG.enslavedDurMs/2)` → 14500 ms: raw phase 0.5, eased 0.5; Virginia frame = 7.5; every tile's scale still 1 (frame-vs-area assertion).
- P7 frames complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tEnslavedMs + CONFIG.enslavedDurMs)` → 15000 ms: every South frame = its enslavedPx (full predicate, all 7), every North frame 0 (all 5), scales 1.
- P8 final state: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)` → 18500 ms: frames = P7 frames; enslavedLabelOpacity 0; freeLabelOpacity 0.
- P9 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to P8 state. durationMs = 21000.
- **Fixed census-instant probes (C*, build instant = census seg-rel − 6000; each evaluated state is CONFIG-derived and the timing swap is shown moving the corresponding phase probes):** C@2000 (census 8000, small-tile) — scale = smallFraction, freeP 0. C@4000 (census 10000, mid-growth) — 0 < freeP < 1 AND arrowsP = 1 AND 0 < freeLabelP < 1. C@6000 (census 12000, free complete) — state equal to P3's tile/label state. C@10000 (census 16000, label present at label-out start) — freeLabelOpacity 1. C@12000 (census 18000, label gone) — freeLabelOpacity 0. C@16000 (census 22000, enslaved complete) — frames = P7 frames AND enslavedLabelP 1. C@20000 (census 26000, final hold) — frames = P7 frames AND enslavedLabelOpacity 0.

