- A6 legs: fit-table.md (PIL rendered measurement, stand-in font DejaVu Serif named — measured ink bounds, never a scaled-font-size claim — for camp headers, centre labels, enslaved label, and all 12 tile labels at their CONFIG fonts, plus neighbouring-label clearance) + config-census.md (all literals classified; every CONFIG key incl. `tiles[]` nested keys resolved to value-flowing sites; CSS-variable check — none used).
- jev-prewave after legs 1–3 + A6, payload per its contract (A6 outputs verbatim, A10.1); five-lens Codex wave (motion · timing · purity · reusability · readability) only on FIRE-WAVE; bar avg ≥85, min ≥70.

### 2.5 Failure points (priced)
- Fitting limits: tile labels at phone width — the fit-floor cure raises small-tile labels above specimen proportion: label font = clamp(freeW × 0.17, 20, 30) px at the 640 stage; Delaware's label (44 px tile, 20 px font) overflows its tile symmetrically, centred, with a CONFIG halo (labelHaloPx) — a named departure from the specimen, measured in the fit leg by PIL ink bounds (the T212 font-raise precedent). The 11.2 px figure is a NOMINAL scaled font size only; the leg's evidence is measured ink.
- Geometry collisions: tile slots amended at §2b to zero tile-vs-tile overlap at full size; the harness asserts it at default AND swap configurations, frames included in stage bounds.
- Allocation-vs-census timing: the t=0 allocation discards the map lead-in's 6 s and T219's 7 s tail; if a timing lens prices the build against the full 34 s window instead of the tile lifecycle, the departure table (§2.3) is the priced answer, filed before the wave.
- Frame-vs-area confusion: the enslaved act must read as ADDED population (frame outside the free tile), never as a resize — frames draw behind the tile rect and grow outward only; tile scale stays 1 through SB-E/F (asserted in P6/P7).
- Camp-assignment dispute: New Jersey's centre-column placement is priced as South by stage half (§1.3); a lens reading it as North is answered by the census column position, filed here in advance.
- Silhouette absence: tiles carry no state outlines (named deferral §2.2 (2)); the readability/motion lenses may price the plainer tile — accepted risk, the name label carries identity.
- Render-proof limitation: no browser binary in this seat — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md; comparison page is the render surface.
- Plateau (A2): FIRST ATTEMPT — no prior average; a FAIL files its WHY in scores.md and routes attempt 2 to practice. **Predicted minimum lens: motion fidelity** (codex-plan-review concurs, citing T210's motion 72 as the family precedent) — hypothesis: the specimen's growth is a continuous area morph while the build interpolates uniform scale about each tile centre, and the omitted silhouettes/map lead-in are motion-visible departures. **Readability priced as a separate floor risk** (codex-plan-review cure, applied): small-tile labels at phone width are the second candidate minimum until the fit leg measures actual ink bounds and collisions; if the wave's minimum is neither, the WHY section names the actual stuck lens and its cause instead.

