**HOLD — ASSERTED-CHECKS.** T218’s filed receipts leave Observe checkpoints unmapped and omit raw results for several assertions in the amended Plan.

| Dimension | Score |
|---|---:|
| Parameterization | 0.90 |
| Purity pre-check | 1.00 |
| Own-checks completeness | 0.35 |
| Fidelity-plan honesty | 0.85 |

## Findings

1. **A11 coverage is incomplete.** The receipt index lists the Plan’s named probes, but Observe §1.3 also records in-scope checkpoints CP7, CP10 and CP12 at build times 8,000, 14,000 and 18,000 ms after subtracting the 6,000 ms allocation. None has an identified executable assertion. The fine checkpoints also need explicit receipt mappings, including where a phase probe can serve both purposes. An independent evaluation of the filed CONFIG shows that F-9000 maps to 3,000 ms, when free growth is already at raw progress `0.2` and eased progress `0.08`. Observe records small tiles holding there. The cure is a checkpoint-to-assertion index with CONFIG expressions, evaluated instants and raw results for each in-scope checkpoint, plus a schedule correction or an explicit disposition for the F-9000 discrepancy. The existing Plan §2.3 departures cover CP0–CP2 and CP14–CP17. [Observe/Plan §§1.3 and 2.3](../../../study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T218-observe-plan.md#23-census-anchor-mapping-a102--a11-assertions) · [Build record §5](build-record.md#5-receipt-index-a13--reconciled-before-payload-assembly)

2. **A12/A13 receipt entries overstate what the harness prints.** P6 and P7 print frame thicknesses and omit the planned all-tile scale predicate. C@16000 and C@20000 print label values and omit the planned frame equality against P7. The timing swap does demonstrate that P6 and P7 move by 1,000 ms. It does not demonstrate the claimed frame change at C@16000. Independent evaluation at 16,000 ms gives the same 12 frame values in both configurations, while enslaved-label progress changes from `1` to `0`. `MOVE@15000` measures a different instant. The cure is a fresh hash-bound harness receipt that prints the complete predicates and the default and swapped observations at each cited instant, with the swapped CONFIG fields and evaluated expressions. [Build record §2, P6–P7, C@16000/C@20000 and swap outputs](build-record.md#2-own-checks--raw-harness-output-a94-harness--node-config--logic-scripts-extracted-from-recreationhtml-and-evaluated-via-vm)

3. **The fit table names a valid proxy instrument, but its geometry record is incomplete.** The filed method identifies Pillow and DejaVu Serif. I reproduced the reported bounding-box dimensions for South, Virginia, Pennsylvania and Massachusetts. Rows 1–7 give zone names and checkmarks without numeric container bounds or binding margins. Row 18 carries Massachusetts as contained, but its filed 180 px proxy width centred at CONFIG `cx=562` reaches approximately `652` on the 640 px stage under the table’s own centring convention. The cure is to file the post-fit position, container bounds and signed margin per row, and carry the Massachusetts proxy overflow explicitly if it remains. [Fit table, instrument and rows 1–7 and 18](fit-table.md) · [Measured-fit guard, checks 1–2](../../../study-jobs/recreation/guards/guard-measured-fit.md)

4. **CONFIG and construction support parameterization and purity.** Tile geometry, phase timing, label content, palette and arrow geometry flow into the SVG from CONFIG. The construction record and source-reference scan show generation from those values. Reusability has a narrower gap: `framePx` uses `enslavedPx` without consulting `camp`, and the content swap gives both North tiles zero thickness. That swap verifies the supplied values, while a South-only rule across configurations would require a validator or an explicit camp predicate and a swap that exercises it. [Recreation CONFIG and `stateAt`](recreation.html) · [Build record §2, `SWAP-CONTENT`](build-record.md)

5. **The fidelity plan names its departures and follows the binding source interpretation.** Observe prices the arrows as rule announcements and keeps the tiles in their camps, with free population shown by area and enslaved population by added frames. The build record names the map, silhouettes and three-fifths tail as deferrals. Its independent arrow-phase claim is only partly supported by the renderer. The free arrow path opacity follows `freeLabelOpacity`, and the arrowhead waits for full label opacity. At C@4000 the receipt shows `arrowsP=1` and label progress about `0.222`, which proves path completion in state but leaves visible arrow completion unproved. The record could state that coupling explicitly or file a renderer-level receipt for the behaviour prescribed in the Plan. [Observe/Plan §§1.2–1.3 and 2.2](../../../study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [Build record §4](build-record.md#4-fidelity-plan-implemented--deferred) · [Recreation `render`](recreation.html)

**Limits** — This is a paperwork verdict with selected Node and Pillow checks against the filed build. Continuous specimen playback, browser pixels and the builder’s complete harness execution were not independently verified.

