## Findings

1. **Three fine checkpoints are credited to receipts at different instants.** The binding allocation in Observe/Plan §2.3 subtracts 6,000 ms. F-11000 therefore maps to 5,000 ms and can use P3 once its full-state receipt is complete. The index assigns it to C@6000. F-21000 maps to 15,000 ms, while its receipt runs at 15,500 ms. Independent evaluation shows enslaved-label progress is `0` at 15,000 and `0.5` at 15,500, so the substitution changes the result. F-27000 maps to 21,000 ms and is credited to C@20000. File the results at the bound instants and record an explicit timing departure if the F-21000 mid-reveal is intentionally placed 500 ms later. [Observe/Plan §§1.3, 2.3](../../../study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [Build record §§2, 5](build-record.md#2-own-checks--raw-harness-output-a94-harness--node-config--logic-scripts-extracted-from-recreationhtml-and-evaluated-via-vm)

2. **Several populated entries still lack the evidence A11–A13 require.** The enslaved timing swap receipts P6 moving `14500→15500` and P7 moving `15000→16000`. The fixed C probes generally print timestamps and state values without a CONFIG-derived evaluation expression or a paired probe shown moving under a relevant timing swap. The Plan’s fixed-source probes are compatible with the call as source-alignment evidence alongside the required moving probes. The printed predicates also remain partial. Z0 omits header opacity, P1 omits tile and header opacity, P3 omits the all-tile scale result, P5 omits free-label opacity, and P8 omits both label opacities. File a final-build harness receipt for each full predicate, with evaluated CONFIG expressions and default-to-swapped instants for the paired phase probes. [Observe/Plan §2.3](../../../study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T218-observe-plan.md#23-census-anchor-mapping-a102--a11-assertions) · [Build record §§2, 5](build-record.md#5-receipt-index-a13--reconciled-before-payload-assembly) · [Recreation INSTRUCTION, A11–A13](../../../study-jobs/recreation/INSTRUCTION.md#amendment-a11-2026-11-17-cycle-028-condense--census-checkpoint-assertions-adopting-the-practice-jobs-census-checkpoint-note-practice-cycle-019-condense-carried-as-a-candidate-by-cycle-027-91-and-adopted-here-on-three-independent-demonstrations)

3. **The named Pillow proxy is valid, but some rows do not measure the final fitted text.** The New Hampshire row measures one line. The SVG renders `New` and `Hampshire` on separate lines, so the filed string width and height cannot establish the fitted ink bounds. The Virginia row measures at `29.7 px`, while the final CONFIG evaluates to `140 × 0.22 = 30.8 px` at full scale. The camp and centre-label rows also leave position and signed margins blank. Re-measure the final spans at their CONFIG-derived sizes and baselines, then file the container bounds and binding margins. The carried proxy overflows can be priced once those measurements are bound to the final geometry. [Fit table, raw rows and HITs](fit-table.md) · [Recreation, `tileFontPx`, `labelLines` and `render`](recreation.html:76) · [Measured-fit guard, checks 1–2](../../../study-jobs/recreation/guards/guard-measured-fit.md)

4. **The other dimensions clear the prewave floors.** CONFIG drives the scene geometry, content, palette and timing. The source-free SVG construction and filed purity scan support the purity pre-check. `SWAP-CONTENT` exercises a North tile with nonzero `enslavedPx` and records a zero frame, and `ARROW-RENDER@4000` records both free arrow paths at full opacity during the partial label reveal. The fidelity record follows the priced interpretation of arrows as rule announcements and names the map lead-in, state silhouettes and T219 tail as deferrals. [Build record §§2, 4, 6](build-record.md) · [Recreation](recreation.html) · [Observe/Plan §§1.2–1.3, 2.2](../../../study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T218-observe-plan.md)

